~ mother_second_meeting_start
(The path grows quiet. The air feels heavy.)

Mother (soft, distant): …You’re bleeding.

- I’ll be fine. => mother_2_response
- …Mother? => mother_2_response
- …(silent) => mother_2_response


~ mother_2_response
Mother (kneeling, though her feet never touch the ground): You always said that.
Mother: Even when your hands shook.
Mother: Even when you were afraid.

- I don’t remember being afraid. => mother_memory
- I don’t remember you. => mother_memory
- I remember pain. => mother_memory


~ mother_memory
Mother (sad smile): Of course you don’t.
Mother: Fear is the first thing the armor takes.
Mother: Pain is what it leaves behind.

Mother: Do you know why I never stopped you?

- Why? => mother_reason
- You should have stopped me. => mother_reason
- …(silent) => mother_reason


~ mother_reason
Mother (quietly): Because you were kind.
Mother: And kind children believe strength can protect everyone.
Mother: Even when it destroys them.

Mother (looking at the armor): That weight… it wasn’t meant for a heart like yours.

- Then why am I still wearing it? => mother_choice
- I don’t know who I am without it. => mother_choice
- …(silent) => mother_choice


~ mother_choice
Mother (voice trembling, but firm): That is what frightens me.
Mother: Not the battles.
Mother: Not the Order.
Mother: But that you might forget how to live without being needed.

Mother (stepping back): Whatever waits ahead…
Mother: Promise me one thing.

- What? => mother_promise
- I can’t promise anything. => mother_promise
- …(silent) => mother_promise


~ mother_promise
Mother (gentle, fading): Don’t disappear again.
Mother: Not into armor.
Mother: Not into duty.
Mother: Not into silence.

Mother: If you must fall…
Mother: Fall as yourself.

(The presence fades. The path forward opens.)

do GameState.mother_end.emit(2)
=> END
